From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:44:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build_seed: fix zero-inode loop detection, stale profiles,
 and zstd metal-sources

Use realpath fallback when directory st_ino is 0 (Windows DirEntry.stat and exFAT volumes) while checking os.lstat and Windows directory reparse points in _verify_no_symlinks_or_unsafe_names and _stage_tree. Validate staged seed profile build versions before mounting DM_GAMES_DIR in _prepare_from_seed, guard report_profile_status against missing build keys, reject mismatched leftover work/profile directories during save_seed/adopt_legacy_work, and clean stale work/profile leftovers on registered seed persistence.

Also stream-compress metal-sources archives as b-<chain>.img.zst with zstd while remaining backward-compatible with legacy .img archives, and add scan-uncompressed and atomic compress-seeds CLI subcommands with full-stream DMROMFS1 header verification and graceful stop handling.

Stream-pack metal-sources directly into zstd without staging an uncompressed .img or loading files via read_bytes(), raise SEED_MAX_BYTES to 128 GiB and SEED_MAX_ENTRIES to 2M for large Switch 2 titles, avoid duplicate decompression and read_bytes() in prepare_prefill, and reject oversized or trailing zstd RomFS bombs at the 32-byte header boundary.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Handle Windows/exFAT zero-inode checks, self-heal stale seed profiles, and stream-compress metal-sources with zstd
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1456, LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1478, LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1618, LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1544
